{"id":"st291-1","designation":"ST 291-1","title":"Ancillary Data — Ancillary Data Packet and Space Formatting","state":"active","suite":"291","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st291-1/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st291-1/","checked_at":"2026-11-11"},"scope":"This standard specifies the basic formatting structure of the ancillary data space in digital video data streams in the form of 10 bit words. Application of this standard includes, but is not limited to, 525-line and 625-line standard definition digital television interfaces (component and composite), high definition digital television interfaces (750 and 1125 lines), and D-Cinema interfaces that provide 8-bit or 10-bit ancillary data spaces. Space available for ancillary data packets is defined in documents specifying connecting interfaces. Ancillary data packet payload definitions for a specific application are specified by a SMPTE Standard, Recommended Practice, or Registered Disclosure Document, or by a document generated by another organization, a company, or an individual (an Entity). When a payload format is registered with SMPTE, an application document describing the payload format is required, and the registered ancillary data packet is identified by a registered data identification word.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"Conformance Notation","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"3 Normative References","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"4 DID and DID/SDID Registration Process","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.1 SMPTE Technology Committees","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.2 Other Organizations, Companies and Individuals (External Entities)","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.3 Registration Request Conflicts","page":6},{"level":1,"title":"Ancillary Data Packet Format","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"5.1 Ancillary Data Packet Types","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"5.2 Component Interface Ancillary Data Packet Format","page":7},{"level":2,"title":"5.3 Composite Interface Ancillary Data Packet Format","page":8},{"level":1,"title":"6 Ancillary Packet Format Data Elements","page":9},{"level":2,"title":"6.1 Data Identification Word (DID) (Type 1 and 2 Data)","page":9},{"level":2,"title":"6.2 Secondary Data Identification Word (SDID) (Type 2 Data only)","page":10},{"level":2,"title":"6.3 Data Identification Word for Deletion of an Ancillary Data Packet","page":11},{"level":2,"title":"6.4 Data Block Number (DBN) (Type 1 Data only)","page":11},{"level":2,"title":"6.5 Data Count (DC)","page":12},{"level":2,"title":"6.6 User Data Words (UDW)","page":12},{"level":2,"title":"6.7 Checksum Word (CS)","page":12},{"level":1,"title":"Ancillary Data Space Formatting (Component or Composite Interface)","page":13},{"level":2,"title":"7.1 Component Data Space","page":13},{"level":2,"title":"7.2 Composite Data Space","page":13},{"level":2,"title":"7.3 Presence, Positioning, and Deletion of Ancillary Data Packets in Available Space","page":13},{"level":1,"title":"8 Exceptions from Ancillary Data Space Formatting","page":14},{"level":2,"title":"8.1 Error Detection and Handling Packet","page":14},{"level":2,"title":"8.2 SDTI Header Packets","page":14},{"level":1,"title":"9 Protected Codes","page":14},{"level":2,"title":"9.1 Ancillary Data Environment","page":14}],"definitions":[],"keywords":[{"term":"Ancillary Data","zh":"辅助数据","abbr":"","category":"tv","source":"curated"},{"term":"EAV","zh":"","abbr":"EAV","category":"other","source":"acronym"},{"term":"SAV","zh":"","abbr":"SAV","category":"other","source":"acronym"},{"term":"ANC","zh":"","abbr":"ANC","category":"other","source":"acronym"},{"term":"DID","zh":"","abbr":"DID","category":"other","source":"acronym"},{"term":"SDID","zh":"","abbr":"SDID","category":"other","source":"acronym"},{"term":"UDW","zh":"","abbr":"UDW","category":"other","source":"acronym"},{"term":"ADF","zh":"","abbr":"ADF","category":"other","source":"acronym"},{"term":"DBN","zh":"","abbr":"DBN","category":"other","so